# Project structure

Home is `app/page.tsx`, the lobby. It is the portal to the experiences. It is not the CV.

The CV is a site page, not an experience. It lives at `app/cv/page.tsx` with its components in `components/cv/`. The shared shell links to `/cv` on every page. The lobby shows the person's name, and that name links to `/cv`.

An experience is one slug:

- route `app/<slug>/page.tsx`, URL `/<slug>`
- components in `components/<slug>/`
- one section in @cyber_playground_roadmap.md
- one rule `.cursor/rules/<slug>.mdc` with `alwaysApply: false` and `globs: app/<slug>/**,components/<slug>/**`

The set of experiences is whatever the roadmap lists. Adding one does not change this rule.

`components/shared/` is the shell: back to the lobby, and the link to `/cv`. Experience folders do not import each other. Static files go in `public/assets/`. No audio files under `public/`.
